  "premise_review": [
    "categorical_trace_cyclic retains exactly {alpha : Type _}, T : Folder.CrystallineTensor.CategoricalTrace alpha and the full original qualified proof call. It genuinely proves the supplied T.cyclic proposition from its original provider's T.cyclic_certified.",
    "The captured CategoricalTrace stores End : Type _, trace : End → Type _, arbitrary cyclic : Prop with proof, and independent unproved additivity?/multiplicativity? propositions. No multiplication, composition, equality of traces or cyclicity equation is encoded by cyclic; alpha is not related to End or trace by a field.",
    "The same provider separately contains an actual Endomorphism.map : alpha → alpha and FixedBy f x := f.map x = x. Those genuine definitions are acknowledged, but this wrapper declares neither and does not establish a connection between them and T.cyclic.",
    "hattori_stallings_trace_defined retains the exact supplied T : Folder.CrystallineTensor.HattoriStallingsTraceContract and original qualified proof call. It genuinely forwards T.traceDefined_certified through the provider, without constructing a trace.",
    "The captured Hattori-Stallings record supplies RingLike/ModuleLike/EndomorphismLike types and traceValue : EndomorphismLike → Type _. It states no ring/module laws, numeric/categorical trace relation or Morita-invariance formula; MoritaInvariant? is an unproved independent Prop.",
    "Both exact genuine proof terms, original parameters, imports, notices and namespaces remain archived. No cyclic trace theorem, Hattori-Stallings construction, Morita result, imported-body completion, type narrowing, new self-provider import, provider substitution or mathematical admission is asserted."
  ],
  "split_decision": "Record the two genuine conditional proof seams separately while preserving their coherent trace-wrapper unit entirely in exact archives. Neither conclusion supplies an independently defined cyclicity or mathematical trace relation to materialize. Do not replace the records, extract imported provider definitions as if source-local, add a new import or reinterpret names as domain laws.",
